Note: Four descriptive precision series per facet: SEMode = model (ModelSE) vs fit_adjusted (RealSE = ModelSE *
sqrt(max(Infit, 1))) crossed with DistributionBasis = sample (ddof=1) vs population (ddof=0). All derived
separation/reliability indices are exploratory summaries (Use = screening_only; SupportsFormalInference = FALSE) and do
not propagate inter-estimate covariance. EstimateAvailable, SEAvailable, ExcludedLevels and AggregationTarget state the
exact calculation scope; JMLE extreme-score boundary persons without finite estimates are excluded explicitly rather
than silently dropped. Strata (H) = (4G+1)/3 is a conceptual index of distinguishable levels, derived from separation G,
not an observed group count or a grouping rule. H = 3 does not establish three actual groups or their cut scores.
Reliability here concerns differentiation, not inter-rater agreement; low rater separation can also reflect imprecision.
Full notes and original technical values are retained in this project.

