Note: FairM and FairZ are model-expected ratings in the original score units, not logits or evidence of fairness. FairM
holds other facet locations at their unweighted fitted means (including the person mean for nonperson targets); FairZ
holds other locations at zero. These are predictions at reference locations, not averages of predictions. PCM uses the
target step-owner's thresholds, or mean thresholds for other targets. An unbounded person mean makes nonperson FairM
unavailable; FairZ remains a distinct zero-reference quantity. Boundary and calibration holds are retained. No
fair-score SE or interval is implemented; logit SEs cannot be reused.
